==== Cut the power method ====

This works too if you had flashed a firmware image from the stock Linksys web interface **and** you've not done another subsequent upgrade from OpenWrt.

Cut the power to the router while the router is booting up.  The router white LED shall blink rapidly and that's when you cut the power--inducing a failed boot.  After 3 failed boots, the EA4500 then boots from the backup partition and reverts back to its Linksys firmware.  [[https://forum.openwrt.org/viewtopic.php?pid=317288#p317288|See Forum]]
